# =============================================================================
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A RULE
#
# Two rules in this file have already cost real time by silently dropping
# files: `*.txt` swallowed all 41,519 ER-Magellan benchmark pairs (git add
# reported nothing, the push looked clean, training failed on the remote with
# "No datasets found"), and a stray `/api` rule left api/schemas.py untracked
# so a fresh clone could not import the API at all.
#
# After editing this file, ALWAYS verify what you actually dropped:
#     git status --short --ignored | Select-String '^!!'
#     git check-ignore -v <some/file/you/expect/to/be/tracked>
#
# Never ignore by bare extension without a matching negation for the data you
# need. Never ignore a *.py source file.
# =============================================================================

# Python
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.Python
*.egg-info/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS / editor junk
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Environment secrets (HF token / RapidAPI / SerpAPI keys)
.env

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bulk text + archives
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `*.txt` exists because text_part_*.txt are ~650 MB scratch dumps. It is a
# blunt rule -- anything genuinely needed must be negated explicitly below.
*.txt
*.zip

# ER-Magellan benchmark pairs are .txt and MUST be tracked: 41,519 human
# labels, a third of the training corpus. Do not remove this negation.
!data/er_magellan/**/*.txt

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trained checkpoints -- never commit
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# trained_model_real/ is ~549 MB. GitHub already warns about a 57 MB blob in
# this repo. The checkpoint is kept as a zip artifact and can be rebuilt in
# ~40 min on a T4 via train_on_real_corpus.py -- see PROJECT_HANDOVER.pdf S7.
# Glob, not a list: every new checkpoint directory was being added by hand and
# trained_model_v8/ (541 MB) had already slipped through the gap.
#
# Contents are excluded rather than the directory itself, so the negation below
# can still work. training_metadata.json MUST stay tracked: it carries
# `serialization` and `inference_threshold`, and a checkpoint missing the first
# silently drops match recall to zero (S2.3 / trap 6.5). It is ~1 KB.
trained_model*/**
!trained_model*/training_metadata.json
trained_model_structured.zip
outputs/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated data -- rebuilt by running the code, don't commit
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FAISS indexes (~165 MB each) and the catalog they index.
data/scale_index/
data/product_index/
data/scale_catalog.jsonl

# Raw WDC downloads (webdatacommons.org, ~21 MB of .json.gz).
50pair/

# Derived from build_real_corpus.py -- regenerate, don't track.
data/real_corpus_train.csv
data/real_corpus_valid.csv

# Audit / candidate-pool artifacts of the dropped WEAKLY_SIMILAR class.
data/audit_weakly_similar.csv
data/_form_factor_product_pool.csv

data/balanced_catalog.csv
data/full_joined_catalog.csv

# Generated deployment bundle (rebuild: python build_deploy.py --model)
deploy/
